# Tech Stack

- Angular 14.x, TypeScript 4.8, RxJS 7
- NgModule architecture — do not introduce standalone components unless migrating the whole app
- SCSS for styles (project default schematic)

# Project Layout

- `src/app/` — feature folders (`chat-features/`, `supervisor/`, `login/`, etc.)
- `src/app/shared/` — `SharedModule`, reusable pipes/components
- `src/app/services/` — injectable services (`providedIn: 'root'`)
- `src/app/models/` — domain interfaces grouped by entity
- `src/app/interceptors/` — HTTP interceptors (e.g. auth)
- No dedicated `core/` module — follow existing flat feature layout

# State Management

- Service-centric state with RxJS `Subject` / `BehaviorSubject` — no NgRx
- Real-time via `socket.io-client` through `socketService`
- Session/config via `sessionStorage` and `appConfigService` (`assets/config.json`)

# HTTP and API

- REST: central `httpService` with `apiEndpoints` map + `HttpClient`
- Base URLs from `appConfigService.config` (GAT, SOCKET, CONVERSATION_MANAGER, etc.)
- Auth: `AuthInterceptor` — Bearer token, `agentId` header, 401 refresh
- GraphQL: `apollo-angular` / `GraphqlService` → conversation-manager GraphQL endpoint
- Do not call `HttpClient` directly from components — use services

# UI Libraries

- Angular Material 14 + PrimeNG 14 (both used via `SharedModule`)
- ngx-translate for i18n
- Match surrounding component library when adding UI (Material vs PrimeNG)

# Components

- Selector prefix: `app-` (kebab-case)
- Component files: `feature-name.component.ts` with PascalCase class + `Component` suffix
- Declare in `AppModule`, `ChatModule`, or `SharedModule` — not standalone

# Routing

- Hash-based routing (`HashLocationStrategy`)
- Lazy-load feature modules via `loadChildren` where existing code does

# Linting and Format

- TSLint + Prettier (`printWidth: 150`, `trailingComma: "none"`)
- Do not introduce ESLint unless the project is being migrated
